You could already create, retrieve, list, and delete segments from the API. Today we're adding[PATCH /segments/:id](https://resend.com/docs/api-reference/segments/update-segment) so you can **rename a segment** the same way.


## Renaming a segment


Pass the segment ID and the new name.


```text
import     {   Resend   }     from     'resend'  ;
const   resend   =     new     Resend  (  're_xxxxxxxxx'  )  ;
const     {   data  ,   error   }     =     await   resend  .  segments  .  update  (        '78261eea-8f8b-4381-83c6-79fa7120f1cf'  ,        {          name  :     'Active Users'  ,        }  ,     )  ;


```


The response confirms the rename:


```text
{        "object"  :     "segment"  ,        "id"  :     "78261eea-8f8b-4381-83c6-79fa7120f1cf"     }
```


Renaming segments is also available in the[Resend CLI](https://resend.com/docs/cli) and through the[MCP server](https://resend.com/docs/mcp-server) .
